1. Scope and definitions

"Software" means the Pixel Perfect / PixlPrfct code, documentation, and other
project material expressly offered under this license. "Modified Software"
means modifications of the Software and works incorporating its code, in source
or compiled form. It includes renamed forks, ports, and embedded copies.
"Licensor" means each copyright holder offering their material under this
license. "You" means the person or organization exercising these permissions.

"Output" means websites, applications, designs, artwork, animations, documents,
and other work you create USING the Software, rather than by incorporating or
modifying the editor's implementation. Output includes code and assets generated
by the Software's ordinary export functions, including SVG animation players and
HTML/CSS runtime helpers, when used to display, animate, or operate your exported
work. Copying the editor, engine, server, or other implementation into a product
is not Output merely because you also used the editor to create that product.

